Hermit kernel (hermit-rs tag hermit-0.13.0, kernel ef27b79): the virtio console
as a byte channel, for Chitala's Native partitioning spike (N1.4).

A guest of the spike talks to the guest beside it through its virtio console,
which the VMM joins to a relay. Upstream, a virtio console replaces the UART
as the console, so kernel log lines would reach the channel, and the console's
stdin echoes what it reads. With this patch the console stays on the UART, and
the virtio console is the file /dev/chitala-channel: reads hand over whole
packets through a buffer, writes go out in packets, and nothing is echoed.
Without a virtio console nothing changes. native/run.sh applies it after the
RNDR patch; it is carried (spike-only) and not proposed upstream as it is.

